            <ArticleTitle>Detection of R576 interleukin-4 receptor an allele gene, serum interleukin-4, and eosinophilic cationic protein in atopic dermatitis patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>31-5</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.4103/0019-5154.48983</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Atopic dermatitis (AD) is a chronic pruritic skin disease. It results from a complex interplay between strong genetic and environmental factors. The aim of this work was to study some biochemical markers of the dermatosis. This included detection of R576 interleukin-4 receptor alpha allele gene. Twenty five patients with AD and 25 controls participated in this study.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
